{"name":"Strawberry Cheesecake","hex":"#ffdbe9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strawberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sweet, usually red, edible accessory fruit of certain plants of the genus Fragaria.","Any plant of the genus Fragaria (that bears such fruit)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor of strawberries.","Flavored with ethyl methylphenylglycidate, an artificial compound which is said to resemble the taste of strawberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry"},{"term":"cheesecake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pie made of sweetened and flavoured cottage cheese or cream cheese, eggs and milk on a crunchy base.","A pie made of cream, eggs and milk (somewhat resembling the modern American chess cake)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheesecake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheesecake","blocks":[{"text":"Cheesecake is a dessert made with a soft fresh cheese, and sugar, with either eggs or cream depending if it is to be baked or not. It may have a crust or base made from crushed cookies, digestive biscuits, graham crackers, pastry, or sometimes sponge cake. Cheesecake is known for its rich, creamy flavor and smooth texture. It may be baked or unbaked and is usually served chilled."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Baked_cheesecake_with_raspberries_and_blueberries.jpg/330px-Baked_cheesecake_with_raspberries_and_blueberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheesecake","wikidata":"Q215348"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry","wikidata":"Q13158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/South-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG/500px-South-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/South-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG/1280px-South-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/South-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG/500px-South-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"South African rose cheesecake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouth-African_Rose_baked_Cheese_Cake.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Japanese_no-bake_cheesecake.jpg/500px-Japanese_no-bake_cheesecake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Japanese_no-bake_cheesecake.jpg/500px-Japanese_no-bake_cheesecake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Japanese no-bake cheesecake (known in Japan as rare cheesecake), garnished with strawberry sauce","link":"